1
00:00:39,748 --> 00:00:41,166
Me? Maid of honor?

2
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:42,917
It can’t be anyone.

3
00:00:43,001 --> 00:00:44,836
It has to be you.

4
00:00:44,919 --> 00:00:47,088
I don't really know anyone else here.

5
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:49,924
Let me know, okay?

6
00:00:57,682 --> 00:00:58,850
- What?
- News?

7
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:08,818
She's getting married.

8
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:13,490
<i>It's just… It doesn't really suit us.</i>

9
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:15,950
Do you have any other options?

10
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:22,624
I gave you all those ideas,
and you didn't like a single one.

11
00:01:22,707 --> 00:01:24,000
Let's think of something else.

12
00:01:24,083 --> 00:01:25,502
Where are the bats around here?

13
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:26,878
Maybe they're the ones
who want to get married.

14
00:01:29,297 --> 00:01:31,424
Sir. You wanted to see me?

15
00:01:38,097 --> 00:01:43,102
It means I'll have to let go
half of our personnel,

16
00:01:43,186 --> 00:01:44,896
starting today!

17
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:49,567
Boring?

18
00:01:49,651 --> 00:01:51,194
You want boring, huh?

19
00:02:03,039 --> 00:02:04,874
You don't even have to imagine it.

20
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:06,292
Because you already know, Mikoy.

21
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:09,003
how weddings are usually done here.

22
00:02:10,421 --> 00:02:12,715
The chairs go here, right here.

23
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:14,968
The pastor stands here.

24
00:02:15,051 --> 00:02:17,053
Then the bride makes her entrance

25
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:19,222
on a raft with a giant heart.

26
00:02:19,305 --> 00:02:22,517
Or over here, on a pedal boat!

27
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,644
Whatever suits your taste.

28
00:02:24,727 --> 00:02:26,688
And since I work here,

29
00:02:26,771 --> 00:02:28,606
I can get you an employee discount.

30
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:29,858
Just like that!

31
00:02:29,941 --> 00:02:32,569
You'll save 20%!

32
00:02:32,652 --> 00:02:35,196
And there are freebies too!
Free pili nuts.

33
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,698
They're delicious, sweetheart.

34
00:02:40,785 --> 00:02:43,830
But of course, we should look
at other options too, right?

35
00:02:43,913 --> 00:02:47,750
Because this place feels
a little too peaceful.

36
00:02:47,834 --> 00:02:51,504
You know, our love story
has always been pretty epic!

37
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:54,173
Pretty epic, you say?

38
00:02:58,177 --> 00:03:02,932
A place where
you won't just say, "I love you."

39
00:03:03,474 --> 00:03:06,978
Instead, you'll say, "I lava you!"

40
00:03:10,398 --> 00:03:11,274
There?

41
00:03:12,191 --> 00:03:13,192
At Mayon Volcano's crater?

42
00:03:14,694 --> 00:03:16,321
- I know someone who can get us
- Sweetheart!

43
00:03:16,404 --> 00:03:19,991
inside the six-kilometer danger zone.

44
00:03:20,074 --> 00:03:22,744
And guess what? We're in luck.

45
00:03:22,827 --> 00:03:25,246
Mayon has been acting up lately.

46
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:26,289
Just imagine.

47
00:03:26,372 --> 00:03:29,792
If we're lucky your wedding backdrop

48
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:32,670
will be flowing lava!

49
00:03:34,714 --> 00:03:37,425
As if your love is burning hot.

50
00:03:37,508 --> 00:03:41,429
A love forged in lava!

51
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:49,062
Come on, say it. Say, "I love you."

52
00:03:50,855 --> 00:03:53,358
Not like that! Like this.

53
00:03:53,441 --> 00:03:56,194
I have to show you.
Come on, let go of that for a second.

54
00:03:56,277 --> 00:03:57,278
Come here, come here.

55
00:03:57,362 --> 00:03:59,447
Over here. Excuse me for a moment.

56
00:04:00,198 --> 00:04:01,574
Just let go of that.

57
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:05,328
Now say, "I love you."

58
00:04:08,873 --> 00:04:11,084
That's it! Perfect!

59
00:04:13,544 --> 00:04:15,505
- I told you.
- Now that's memorable!

60
00:04:17,715 --> 00:04:21,719
Why does it have to be memorable?
I just want to get married.

61
00:04:21,803 --> 00:04:23,096
I don't want to die.

62
00:04:24,222 --> 00:04:27,100
Die? You're so negative, dear.

63
00:04:27,725 --> 00:04:30,270
I'm not being negative. It's a fact.

64
00:04:30,853 --> 00:04:33,273
There's a reason there's
a permanent danger zone

65
00:04:33,356 --> 00:04:34,732
around Mayon Volcano.

66
00:04:34,816 --> 00:04:37,777
I don't want to get married
while the volcano is active.

67
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:42,573
You're so picky.

68
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:44,242
So what is it that you want?

69
00:04:46,035 --> 00:04:47,203
Yes, sweetheart.

70
00:04:47,954 --> 00:04:49,205
What do you want?

71
00:05:09,642 --> 00:05:11,102
It just reminded me of…

72
00:05:14,647 --> 00:05:16,649
The first church you ever took me to.

73
00:05:17,692 --> 00:05:19,402
Is this where you want it?

74
00:05:19,485 --> 00:05:22,655
You know, statistically speaking,

75
00:05:22,739 --> 00:05:24,324
couples who get married in church,

76
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:26,701
- are--
- Ma'am.

77
00:05:26,784 --> 00:05:28,286
What if…

78
00:05:29,370 --> 00:05:30,330
you head over there first?

79
00:05:30,413 --> 00:05:32,290
To that permanent danger zone
you mentioned.

80
00:05:32,373 --> 00:05:34,876
- Sure.
- Why don't you let us have a moment alone?

81
00:05:34,959 --> 00:05:35,960
All right, all right.

82
00:05:36,044 --> 00:05:37,962
- Okay?
- Off to the lava!

83
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:42,925
All right, then.
I'll wait for you in the van.

84
00:05:43,009 --> 00:05:44,052
Yes, ma'am.

85
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:45,136
It's so hot.

86
00:05:48,848 --> 00:05:51,768
‪RED LABUYO
‪RESTAURANT

87
00:06:03,279 --> 00:06:05,907
I know you're not really
the traditional type, but…

88
00:06:27,678 --> 00:06:28,596
Why?

89
00:06:33,434 --> 00:06:36,312
It just reminded me of Mom and Dad.

90
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:45,988
They're far from perfect,

91
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:49,242
and to be honest,

92
00:06:50,493 --> 00:06:53,996
they're actually the reason
my life became such a mess.

93
00:06:56,749 --> 00:06:59,043
But whenever I picture myself

94
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:02,296
saying my vows

95
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:04,632
before the altar,

96
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:08,136
standing in front of the love of my life…

97
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:13,516
they should be there, shouldn't they?

98
00:07:16,811 --> 00:07:18,438
Because no matter what happened,

99
00:07:21,107 --> 00:07:23,234
they're still my parents.

100
00:07:32,702 --> 00:07:34,871
Maybe there's still a chance
they'll be there.

101
00:07:39,417 --> 00:07:40,877
I've stopped hoping.

102
00:07:46,549 --> 00:07:48,009
Don't give up just yet.

103
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,137
We'll find a way.

104
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:58,144
I promise I'll do everything I can

105
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:00,855
just to give you everything you want.

106
00:08:05,193 --> 00:08:08,446
You shouldn't make promises
in front of the Blessed Mother!

107
00:08:08,529 --> 00:08:09,697
Why not?

108
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,324
Because you have to keep them.

109
00:08:11,407 --> 00:08:12,408
Exactly!

110
00:08:12,492 --> 00:08:14,827
Nuestra Señora, I truly mean it.

111
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:16,537
I'll give her everything.

112
00:08:17,997 --> 00:08:19,540
As long as Chiara is happy.

113
00:08:24,045 --> 00:08:25,254
I really do.

114
00:08:43,648 --> 00:08:45,775
What? Do we really need one?

115
00:08:45,858 --> 00:08:49,028
Where I'm from,
everyone's invited to a wedding.

116
00:08:49,111 --> 00:08:50,863
The whole barangay can come?

117
00:08:51,447 --> 00:08:52,782
And everyone gets to eat?

118
00:08:52,865 --> 00:08:54,700
Then why don't we invite
all my online followers?

119
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:58,663
We can turn it into one huge
social media event!

120
00:08:58,746 --> 00:09:00,790
Wait a minute!

121
00:09:00,873 --> 00:09:01,832
Hold on.

122
00:09:02,542 --> 00:09:03,543
Are you paying for it?

123
00:09:04,502 --> 00:09:05,920
Are you feeding everyone?

124
00:09:06,629 --> 00:09:08,089
This is a wedding.

125
00:09:08,172 --> 00:09:09,799
Not a feeding program.

126
00:09:09,882 --> 00:09:13,344
She has a point.
Leonela's absolutely right.

127
00:09:13,928 --> 00:09:15,221
Before you know it,

128
00:09:15,304 --> 00:09:17,557
they'll be starting their marriage

129
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:19,725
- buried in debt.
- Exactly.

130
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:20,768
- You're right.
- See?

131
00:09:20,851 --> 00:09:21,727
What we should do

132
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:24,230
is invite only the people
who are truly close to the family.

133
00:09:24,313 --> 00:09:25,106
Right, right.

134
00:09:25,189 --> 00:09:27,608
That way, their special moment

135
00:09:28,192 --> 00:09:30,319
stays solemn and meaningful.

136
00:09:30,903 --> 00:09:33,364
Exactly. Let's keep it small and intimate.

137
00:09:48,129 --> 00:09:49,589
What's going on?

138
00:09:49,672 --> 00:09:51,549
We already know what's bothering you.

139
00:09:52,633 --> 00:09:56,178
And we also know exactly
what answer you're looking for.

140
00:09:56,262 --> 00:09:57,513
That's why we're here.

141
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:59,932
We've been brainstorming
about your problem,

142
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:01,726
trying to find the answer.

143
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:05,313
You already know what I need?

144
00:10:18,159 --> 00:10:19,160
Now…

145
00:10:19,243 --> 00:10:24,040
We've gathered here today
to solve a very pressing issue.

146
00:10:24,749 --> 00:10:25,708
Namely,

147
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:30,379
whether or not Agent Alex should agree
to be the maid of honor

148
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:32,006
at Mikoy and Chiara's wedding.

149
00:10:32,089 --> 00:10:32,923
Exactly.

150
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:36,677
But you know--

151
00:10:39,889 --> 00:10:41,307
Don't say anything.

152
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:48,773
Actually, I talked to Mikoy earlier.

153
00:10:57,323 --> 00:11:01,285
Hey! Can you calm down first, Carlota?

154
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:04,288
Mikoy, I can't believe
you're getting married!

155
00:11:04,372 --> 00:11:08,167
Imagine, I only called
to recruit you into an MLM.

156
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:10,711
<i>Then I found out you're getting married!</i>

157
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:12,713
Whoa, take it easy.

158
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:15,132
More importantly, have you talked
to Agent Alex yet?

159
00:11:15,216 --> 00:11:16,759
Agent Alex?

160
00:11:17,635 --> 00:11:21,472
Mikoy, don't tell me
you're getting married,

161
00:11:21,555 --> 00:11:23,641
and only now you've started
having a crush on Agent Alex?

162
00:11:25,601 --> 00:11:27,395
What are you talking about?

163
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:32,191
And that is how I learned
that Chiara asked Agent Alex

164
00:11:32,274 --> 00:11:35,027
to be her maid of honor.

165
00:11:35,611 --> 00:11:39,365
And that is why this meeting is necessary

166
00:11:39,448 --> 00:11:44,829
because Agent Alexandria Cortez
needs our advice.

167
00:11:44,912 --> 00:11:49,083
She needs our guidance, our support,

168
00:11:49,166 --> 00:11:52,628
to lead her down the right path.

169
00:11:52,711 --> 00:11:54,672
- Amen!
- Given our problem,

170
00:11:54,755 --> 00:11:59,218
we need to conduct a SWOT analysis
of this situation.

171
00:12:01,470 --> 00:12:04,223
We need to carefully analyze

172
00:12:04,306 --> 00:12:06,225
- the strengths, weaknesses,
- Strengths, weaknesses…

173
00:12:06,308 --> 00:12:12,314
opportunities, and threats
of Agent Alex becoming the maid of honor.

174
00:12:14,984 --> 00:12:17,695
As for me, as long
as we're all together, I'm happy.

175
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:20,489
- That's it!
- Then why don't we invite Betchay

176
00:12:20,573 --> 00:12:23,742
and everyone we used to hang out with
back in Cebu?

177
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:25,661
- Right?
- That’s right.

178
00:12:25,744 --> 00:12:29,290
If we're inviting Betchay,
then we should invite Buddy Pato too.

179
00:12:29,373 --> 00:12:31,375
- Also Buddy Georgie and Raul.
- Right!

180
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:35,337
Buddy Max, right?
Buddy Raul and Luis should be there too.

181
00:12:35,921 --> 00:12:37,089
- Brother Luis.
- So, then…

182
00:12:37,173 --> 00:12:40,217
Then let's invite everyone
from our Legion of Mary group too.

183
00:12:40,301 --> 00:12:41,719
We're close to a lot of them.

184
00:12:45,097 --> 00:12:46,432
And then Sister Jessie.

185
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:48,893
What about the barangay officers,
Aunt Tess?

186
00:12:48,976 --> 00:12:50,603
Just let me know so I can inform them.

187
00:12:50,686 --> 00:12:52,855
They might get offended
if they're left out.

188
00:12:52,938 --> 00:12:53,814
Good point.

189
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:56,484
And if the barangay officers are coming,

190
00:12:56,567 --> 00:12:58,277
then our whole gang should be there too.

191
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:00,237
The Gala group and Loopers.

192
00:13:01,071 --> 00:13:02,823
Hold on!

193
00:13:03,824 --> 00:13:06,660
I thought we agreed to invite
only close family?

194
00:13:07,536 --> 00:13:10,289
At this rate, we might as well invite
the Senate

195
00:13:10,372 --> 00:13:11,665
and the House of Representatives!

196
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:13,542
Sounds like you want to invite
the whole Philippines!

197
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:15,294
I never thought of that, Leonela.

198
00:13:15,377 --> 00:13:16,504
That's a great idea!

199
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:23,052
Invite them too. They give amazing gifts!

200
00:13:23,135 --> 00:13:24,887
And where does the money come from?

201
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:27,056
- From the suitcase!
- From the suitcase!

202
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:29,391
Jackpot!

203
00:13:29,475 --> 00:13:32,019
Yes, we can have Senator Quintin
take care of that!

204
00:13:32,102 --> 00:13:33,103
Yes. Right.

205
00:13:33,187 --> 00:13:34,355
What about the GAGO?

206
00:13:35,481 --> 00:13:36,649
Enough!

207
00:13:36,732 --> 00:13:38,609
Stop this wedding at once!

208
00:13:44,823 --> 00:13:47,743
Let's start with S, for strength.

209
00:13:48,953 --> 00:13:51,497
Okay, strength. I like this SWOT idea.

210
00:13:53,165 --> 00:13:55,876
One of Agent Alex's strengths

211
00:13:55,960 --> 00:14:00,214
is maintaining her bond
and connection with Mikoy and Chiara.

212
00:14:00,798 --> 00:14:02,675
And as the maid of honor,

213
00:14:02,758 --> 00:14:05,636
she'll officially remain
a part of their lives.

214
00:14:05,719 --> 00:14:07,680
Because as they say,

215
00:14:07,763 --> 00:14:09,765
"Bonds make us stronger."

216
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:22,987
Especially since Agent Alex always gets
dragged into Mikoy and Chiara's drama.

217
00:14:23,571 --> 00:14:25,072
Not to mention,

218
00:14:25,155 --> 00:14:26,699
Alex might get demoralized

219
00:14:26,782 --> 00:14:30,160
because Mikoy is the one that got away.

220
00:14:31,537 --> 00:14:32,705
Come on, Dara.

221
00:14:33,372 --> 00:14:36,083
Wait, wait. We have an O-pportunity.

222
00:14:36,166 --> 00:14:39,003
If you agree to be the maid of honor,

223
00:14:39,086 --> 00:14:43,132
you'll know their every move
and where Mikoy and Chiara are.

224
00:14:45,092 --> 00:14:48,762
You'll find out if she ever goes back
to her life in the syndicate.

225
00:14:50,389 --> 00:14:54,143
- That's a great o-pportunity.
- "Oh", right.

226
00:14:57,521 --> 00:14:58,522
But!

227
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:01,025
There's a threat.

228
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:03,777
What threat?

229
00:15:04,361 --> 00:15:08,282
Agent Alex might tempt Mikoy
with her beauty and sex appeal

230
00:15:08,365 --> 00:15:10,743
and ruin their grand wedding.

231
00:15:14,371 --> 00:15:17,374
- You know what you're all missing?
- What?

232
00:15:27,217 --> 00:15:30,596
One thing I will never tolerate
is all this nonsense in the office.

233
00:15:31,263 --> 00:15:34,850
And if I'm the subject,
that's a different story.

234
00:15:36,769 --> 00:15:39,688
Talk to me when you're finally ready
to get back to work.

235
00:15:50,991 --> 00:15:53,369
- This is all your fault.
- Yours!

236
00:15:54,745 --> 00:15:56,830
E-nough with that already.

237
00:15:57,456 --> 00:16:02,127
<i>E-veryone knows they're getting married</i>

238
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:03,253
But why?

239
00:16:03,337 --> 00:16:05,422
You can't even agree on the guest list.

240
00:16:05,506 --> 00:16:07,299
We can't even agree with each other.

241
00:16:09,051 --> 00:16:10,469
Look.

242
00:16:10,552 --> 00:16:13,305
Have you seen the movie <i>Top Gun</i>?

243
00:16:13,389 --> 00:16:15,683
Oh, perfect! Let's invite Senator Quintin.

244
00:16:16,225 --> 00:16:17,226
- Why?
- What's the connection?

245
00:16:19,436 --> 00:16:20,479
That's not it.

246
00:16:20,562 --> 00:16:22,356
The movie is <i>Top Gun</i>.

247
00:16:22,439 --> 00:16:24,024
Because they said,

248
00:16:24,108 --> 00:16:26,193
"It's not about the plane.

249
00:16:26,276 --> 00:16:27,861
It's about the pilot."

250
00:16:29,071 --> 00:16:30,823
What does that have to do with this?

251
00:16:39,289 --> 00:16:41,625
Leonela's right.

252
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:45,004
You guys are going overboard
with the guest list.

253
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:46,922
You're worse than Taylor Swift.

254
00:16:47,006 --> 00:16:48,090
Taylor Swift.

255
00:16:48,173 --> 00:16:49,550
Tess is up to date!

256
00:16:49,633 --> 00:16:51,593
Well, of course!

257
00:17:00,185 --> 00:17:01,228
But you're right.

258
00:17:01,311 --> 00:17:04,064
Maybe we should only invite the people

259
00:17:04,148 --> 00:17:07,317
who truly have a connection
with Chiara and Mikoy.

260
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:09,403
Not just our friends from

261
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:11,113
Zumba.

262
00:17:12,531 --> 00:17:13,657
Wait a minute.

263
00:17:13,741 --> 00:17:16,410
Chiara, is there anyone
you'd like to invite?

264
00:17:23,125 --> 00:17:24,918
Mommy Tess,

265
00:17:25,002 --> 00:17:28,088
why don't you go ahead and invite
the people you want first.

266
00:17:28,172 --> 00:17:29,131
I'm okay with that.

267
00:17:33,510 --> 00:17:36,805
Next, let's talk about the catering.

268
00:17:36,889 --> 00:17:38,182
- Red snapper.
- I want menudo.

269
00:17:38,265 --> 00:17:39,224
Just red snapper.

270
00:17:39,308 --> 00:17:40,976
- No, there should be menudo!
- Next is the red snapper.

271
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:43,687
Wait, why catering?
I should be the one cooking.

272
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:45,564
Your lumpiang shanghai is delicious.

273
00:17:45,647 --> 00:17:47,691
It's not a wedding
without eggplant omelet.

274
00:17:47,775 --> 00:17:48,609
Right!

275
00:17:48,692 --> 00:17:51,195
- Salted eggs.
- That's my favorite.

276
00:17:51,987 --> 00:17:53,197
What is it, sweetheart?

277
00:17:53,739 --> 00:17:54,948
Are you okay?

278
00:17:55,699 --> 00:17:56,950
I'm okay.

279
00:17:57,618 --> 00:18:00,579
Yes, don't think about it.
They're always like that,

280
00:18:00,662 --> 00:18:02,498
especially when it comes to guest lists.

281
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:05,250
It's actually kind of sweet.

282
00:18:05,334 --> 00:18:07,878
They're just as excited as we are
about our wedding.

283
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:11,965
If they want to invite everyone,
that's okay.

284
00:18:13,258 --> 00:18:14,885
Didn't you hear the wedding planner?

285
00:18:14,968 --> 00:18:18,180
More guests mean more expenses.

286
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:23,727
Sweetheart, we have the rest
of our lives to pay off our debts.

287
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:30,359
Why don't you want to invite
your mom and dad?

288
00:18:31,985 --> 00:18:34,404
You know that's not possible.

289
00:18:34,488 --> 00:18:37,366
Well, I could always talk to Agent Alex.

290
00:18:37,449 --> 00:18:41,120
After all, you invited her
to be your maid of honor.

291
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:43,789
Maybe there's something she can do, right?

292
00:18:43,872 --> 00:18:45,958
She can make that your wedding gift.

293
00:18:47,501 --> 00:18:49,503
But I don't know

294
00:18:50,629 --> 00:18:54,174
how they'll react,
or if your parents will even accept

295
00:18:54,258 --> 00:18:56,176
seeing my parents.

296
00:18:58,178 --> 00:18:59,555
They'll understand.

297
00:19:01,723 --> 00:19:02,808
No matter what happened,

298
00:19:02,891 --> 00:19:05,435
no matter what our families
have been through,

299
00:19:05,519 --> 00:19:07,855
we're one family now,

300
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:11,525
and families always forgive each other.

301
00:19:15,779 --> 00:19:17,865
I know who I want to invite.

302
00:19:19,908 --> 00:19:20,742
That's great.

303
00:19:20,826 --> 00:19:23,078
Anyone's fine, sweetheart.

304
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:24,121
As long as it's your choice.

305
00:19:41,889 --> 00:19:42,973
Bok.

306
00:19:43,849 --> 00:19:44,725
Admit it.

307
00:19:50,647 --> 00:19:53,984
I know you enjoy teasing me
about my dynamic with Mikoy and Chiara.

308
00:19:56,987 --> 00:19:57,905
Wait.

309
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:00,866
Were you really mad at us?

310
00:20:03,243 --> 00:20:04,369
If I were going to be mad,

311
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:06,371
I would've been a long time ago.

312
00:20:09,625 --> 00:20:12,211
Okay, fine. So, how are things?

313
00:20:12,294 --> 00:20:14,213
Have you decided yet?

314
00:20:14,296 --> 00:20:15,672
About Chiara's offer?

315
00:20:17,591 --> 00:20:20,219
I'm not even sure
if that offer was serious.

316
00:20:21,261 --> 00:20:22,429
Bok.

317
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:26,016
Chiara was serious about her offer.
Do you know why?

318
00:20:26,892 --> 00:20:30,646
She has no one, especially now that
both her parents are in jail.

319
00:20:32,564 --> 00:20:33,815
So think it over.

320
00:20:36,693 --> 00:20:39,071
Wait. You mentioned something earlier.

321
00:20:39,613 --> 00:20:43,325
What's the serious issue
between you and General Norberto?

322
00:20:45,786 --> 00:20:47,579
You're finally interested in your job.

323
00:20:48,372 --> 00:20:49,414
What is it?

324
00:20:54,711 --> 00:20:56,129
What's the problem?

325
00:20:56,213 --> 00:20:58,840
Remember when I said
that Senator Quintin keeps pushing

326
00:20:58,924 --> 00:21:01,218
to bring Mikoy and Chiara back
into the agency?

327
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:11,186
Looks like that good senator
is up to something.

328
00:21:25,867 --> 00:21:29,955
Looks like Mikoy wants you
to make your own decision

329
00:21:30,038 --> 00:21:31,373
about whether you'll be

330
00:21:31,456 --> 00:21:34,042
the maid of honor for his soon-to-be wife.

331
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:40,132
Hello?

332
00:21:44,428 --> 00:21:46,847
Donabel and Viktor are being held
in a maximum-security facility.

333
00:21:46,930 --> 00:21:49,474
I'm not asking you to break them out.

334
00:21:49,558 --> 00:21:51,143
I'm just saying,

335
00:21:51,226 --> 00:21:53,687
maybe we could ask the judge for a favor,

336
00:21:53,770 --> 00:21:57,232
<i>so they can at least attend</i>
<i>their daughter's wedding, right?</i>

337
00:22:03,613 --> 00:22:05,741
What you're asking for, Mikoy,
won't be easy.

338
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:08,410
You're right. It won't.

339
00:22:08,493 --> 00:22:10,203
But it's not impossible, is it?

340
00:22:13,915 --> 00:22:15,417
I'll see what I can do.

341
00:22:15,500 --> 00:22:17,085
<i>Do you need anything else?</i>

342
00:22:17,169 --> 00:22:19,254
<i>Want me to do your grocery shopping?</i>

343
00:22:19,838 --> 00:22:23,091
Or maybe wash your car?

344
00:22:23,884 --> 00:22:24,801
Sure!

345
00:22:27,971 --> 00:22:29,473
I'm just kidding.

346
00:22:29,556 --> 00:22:32,142
I don't even have a car
or groceries to buy.

347
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:41,610
All right, I should get back to work.

348
00:22:42,402 --> 00:22:43,779
Uh, Alex.

349
00:22:44,362 --> 00:22:45,363
What is it?

350
00:22:47,657 --> 00:22:48,700
Are we okay?

351
00:22:53,538 --> 00:22:55,582
Is this about what I told you, Mikoy?

352
00:23:01,088 --> 00:23:02,089
Yes.

353
00:23:04,382 --> 00:23:05,759
You know, Mikoy,

354
00:23:07,594 --> 00:23:09,721
I was just being honest about how I feel…

355
00:23:13,141 --> 00:23:15,435
but I wasn't expecting anything.

356
00:23:17,312 --> 00:23:19,147
<i>Even if that's how I feel.</i>

357
00:23:22,526 --> 00:23:23,568
I hope

358
00:23:24,820 --> 00:23:27,322
we can still be friends.

359
00:23:28,657 --> 00:23:31,118
Of course! Absolutely!

360
00:23:31,201 --> 00:23:33,662
Out of all my friends,
you're the most unique!

361
00:23:34,329 --> 00:23:36,331
Because you're the only one
who has a crush on me.

362
00:23:38,166 --> 00:23:39,209
You're ridiculous.

363
00:23:41,670 --> 00:23:42,796
Just kidding.

364
00:23:44,506 --> 00:23:47,050
By the way, congratulations
to you and Chiara.

365
00:24:00,522 --> 00:24:02,065
Thank you, Alex.

366
00:24:24,004 --> 00:24:28,049
Or maybe a better question is,
will you be okay?

367
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:29,217
Of course, Bok!

368
00:24:29,301 --> 00:24:30,927
You have nothing to worry about.

369
00:24:34,139 --> 00:24:35,557
Come on.

370
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:37,225
It's embarrassing.

371
00:24:37,309 --> 00:24:39,519
There won't be anyone
sitting on the bride's side.

372
00:24:39,603 --> 00:24:42,731
And no one comes forward for the picture.
Not even one.

373
00:24:43,565 --> 00:24:46,067
So, are you coming or not?

374
00:24:47,027 --> 00:24:48,486
Norberto.

375
00:24:48,570 --> 00:24:51,198
I heard you're planning to report
Quintin to the Ombudsman.

376
00:24:52,449 --> 00:24:56,203
Because he diverted the agency's budget.
